Falsifies `allocation_cache::verification::a_pop_returns_the_block_last_pushed`.

The defect: `push` links every block to nothing instead of to the block pushed before it, so the
stack forgets everything under its top.

Expected to fail: the harness's claim that the second `pop` returns the first block pushed.

diff --git a/crates/allocation_cache/src/lib.rs b/crates/allocation_cache/src/lib.rs
index 5558eb4ef..18c026361 100644
--- a/crates/allocation_cache/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/allocation_cache/src/lib.rs
@@ -293,7 +293,7 @@ impl Cache {
         // SAFETY: the caller's contract: the block is ours, writable and big and aligned enough.
         unsafe {
             node.write(Free {
-                next: self.heads[class.index()],
+                next: core::ptr::null_mut(),
             });
         };
         self.heads[class.index()] = node;
